DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.21770859
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OPERA-GC, please cite this exact software release and the accompanying article."
title: "OPERA-GC: An operator-aware and selection-preserving framework for heterogeneous globular-cluster proper-motion kinematics"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-03"
type: software
author:
  - family-names: "Turaev"
    given-names: "Sobir"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4932-241X"
    affiliation: "Advanced Researches of Astrophysics, Ulugh Beg Astronomical Institute, Uzbekistan Academy of Sciences, Astronomy 33, Tashkent 100052, Uzbekistan"
abstract: >-
  OPERA-GC is a reproducible Python framework for preserving selection,
  covariance, radial support, reference-frame semantics, provenance, and
  scientific claim gates in heterogeneous HST and Gaia globular-cluster
  proper-motion analyses. This release includes executable stage packages,
  frozen outputs, manuscript source, figures, and integrity metadata.
keywords:
  - globular clusters
  - proper motions
  - scientific software
  - data provenance
  - selection functions
  - uncertainty quantification
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
